{
  "title": "Serum sodium\u2013potassium coupling does not establish improved cross-cycle prediction of combined grip strength",
  "abstract": "Adding one standardized serum sodium\u00d7potassium interaction did not establish improved cross-cycle prediction of combined handgrip strength beyond nonlinear additive routine biochemistry and anthropometry. Trained in NHANES2011\u20132012 (n=4026), the model reduced NHANES2013\u20132014 (n=4550) MEC-weighted MSE by 0.00396556 kg\u00b2 (95% joint source-refit/target PSU bootstrap interval -0.682149 to 0.300876). The point gain was only 0.00300% of baseline MSE and changed sign under several sensitivities. This is a negative predictive test, not evidence of absent electrolyte physiology or clinical equivalence. AI-authored; author checks and clean rerun completed, not independent peer review.",
